<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Giang Vo by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Giang Vo is the event quarter of Ba Dinh, the stretch of the city between the landmark precincts and the modern west where the exhibition grounds, the wide boulevard and the quieter residential blocks give a rental rider a base with a rare balance, close enough to the centre to keep the old map short, far enough west to keep the streets calm, and event-shaped enough to give the calendar its own pull. A stay here is a stay between two Hanois, the formal landmark city on one side and the working west on the other, and the machine is the bridge the whole plan rides on. Planning it honestly is what this page does.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, and every plan on this page starts and ends with that fact. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and the verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/ba-dinh-rental-planning/">Ba Dinh rental planning</a> page for the district-level picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/dong-da-rental-planning/">Dong Da rental planning</a> page for the working district south of the boulevard.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The quarter&rsquo;s position</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The pickup question</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The daily pattern of a stay</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The handover at the counter</a></li>
